  "command": "MNOS_BENCH_DIR=<fresh-directory> MNOS_BENCH_READS=32768 <immutable-import_cost-binary> --ignored --nocapture --exact retained_blob_read_cost",
  "measurement": "Nine quiet release runs, rotating snapshot control, explicit-transaction ObjectReader and implicit-transaction ObjectReader; 128 held files, full verified byte checks each read. No concurrent builds or benchmarks.",
  "variant_definitions": {
    "control": "Permanent protected SQL snapshot; original evaluator strategy.",
    "candidate": "ObjectReader at e14cade; short explicit transaction plus current-state header lookup for each object read.",
    "autocommit": "Same evaluator integration and benchmark as candidate; short implicit record query, generation admitted once, no current-state header query."
  },
  "scope": [
    "Comparison between candidate and autocommit isolates the two Casita SQL source changes. The control binary predates the acquisition-helper refactor; its timed retained-snapshot point-read path is unchanged.",
    "No cache added; no data or pin-ledger writes during timed reads.",
    "New path improves median read time 9.62% for 128-byte files and 6.30% for 4096-byte files relative to explicit-transaction ObjectReader.",
    "It remains 6.05% and 8.23% slower than the permanent-snapshot control. Do not claim universal improvement or an end-to-end NAR gain from this microbenchmark."
  ],
